# Implementation Task: WebSocket Chat Interface for AI OSCE Sessions

## Overview
Implement a real-time chat interface for medical students to practice OSCE (Objective Structured Clinical Examination) scenarios with AI patients.

## Requirements

### Functional Requirements
1. **WebSocket Connection Management**
   - Establish WebSocket connection on component mount
   - Auto-reconnect on connection loss (exponential backoff)
   - Display connection status indicator
   - Clean up connection on component unmount

2. **Message Handling**
   - Send user messages via WebSocket
   - Receive and display AI patient responses
   - Show typing indicators when AI is responding
   - Display message timestamps
   - Support message history scrolling

3. **UI Components**
   - Chat message list with auto-scroll to latest
   - Message input field with Send button
   - Session controls (Start, End, Pause)
   - Connection status indicator
   - Loading states during initialization

4. **Error Handling**
   - Display user-friendly errors for connection failures
   - Handle WebSocket errors gracefully
   - Provide retry mechanism for failed messages
   - Show offline mode indicator

### Technical Constraints

**CRITICAL - READ BEFORE STARTING:**

1. **Existing Code Patterns (MUST FOLLOW)**:
   - Technology Stack: React 19 + TypeScript 5.9 + Material-UI 7 + Vite 7
   - State Management: React Query for server state, React hooks for local state
   - Styling: Material-UI components with custom theme
   - API Client: Axios with interceptors (see frontend/src/api/axios.ts)
   - Example Reference: frontend/src/pages/MCQBrowser.tsx

2. **Performance Requirements**:
   - Message latency: <500ms (p95)
   - UI render time: <100ms
   - Smooth scrolling: 60fps
   - Bundle size: <50KB gzipped for this component

3. **Security Requirements**:
   - NO hardcoded WebSocket URLs (use environment variables)
   - NO localStorage for sensitive data (JWT tokens only in httpOnly cookies)
   - Input sanitization: Sanitize all user messages before rendering
   - XSS prevention: Use Material-UI Text components (auto-escapes)

4. **Accessibility Requirements (WCAG 2.2 AA)**:
   - Keyboard navigation: Tab, Enter, Escape support
   - Screen reader: aria-labels for all interactive elements
   - Focus management: Focus message input after sending
   - High contrast: Support Material-UI high contrast theme

5. **Australian Medical Context**:
   - Use Australian medical terminology (paracetamol not acetaminophen)
   - AMC Clinical Examination format compliance
   - Australian sources references (eTG, AHPRA, AMH)
   - SI units (mmol/L not mg/dL)

### Implementation Steps

1. **Create Component Structure** (2h)
   - Create frontend/src/components/osce/OSCEChatInterface.tsx
   - Define TypeScript interfaces for props and state
   - Set up Material-UI layout (Box, Grid, Paper)
   - Create sub-components (MessageList, MessageInput, SessionControls)

2. **WebSocket Integration** (3h)
   - Implement WebSocket connection logic with useEffect
   - Handle connection lifecycle (connect, disconnect, reconnect)
   - Create message event handlers (onMessage, onError, onClose)
   - Implement auto-reconnect with exponential backoff
   - Add connection status indicator

3. **Message Handling** (2h)
   - Create message state management with useState
   - Implement send message function
   - Add typing indicator logic
   - Implement auto-scroll to latest message
   - Add message timestamp formatting

4. **Testing** (2h)
   - Write unit tests (Vitest + React Testing Library)
   - Write integration tests (mock WebSocket)
   - Write E2E tests (Playwright)
   - Achieve ≥80% code coverage

### Validation Checklist (Complete Before Returning)

**Agent MUST verify ALL of these before marking task complete:**

- [ ] Run `npx tsc --noEmit` → 0 TypeScript errors
- [ ] Run `npm run lint` → 0 ESLint errors
- [ ] Run `npm test -- OSCEChatInterface` → 100% test pass rate
- [ ] Run `grep -r "ws://\|hardcoded\|localhost" src/components/osce/` → 0 matches
- [ ] Manual test: Connect to WebSocket, send/receive messages
- [ ] Manual test: Verify auto-reconnect on connection loss
- [ ] Accessibility audit: `npx playwright test a11y` → 0 violations
- [ ] Performance test: Message latency <500ms

### Code Example (Correct Pattern)

```typescript
import React, { useState, useEffect, useCallback, useRef } from 'react';
import {
  Box,
  Typography,
  TextField,
  Button,
  Paper,
  CircularProgress,
  Alert
} from '@mui/material';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';

// Environment variable for WebSocket URL
const WS_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_WEBSOCKET_URL;

interface Message {
  id: string;
  sender: 'user' | 'ai';
  content: string;
  timestamp: number;
}

interface OSCEChatInterfaceProps {
  sessionId: string;
  personaCode: string;
  onSessionEnd?: () => void;
}

export const OSCEChatInterface: React.FC<OSCEChatInterfaceProps> = ({
  sessionId,
  personaCode,
  onSessionEnd
}) => {
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState<Message[]>([]);
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [isConnected, setIsConnected] = useState(false);
  const [isTyping, setIsTyping] = useState(false);
  const wsRef = useRef<WebSocket | null>(null);
  const messagesEndRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

  // WebSocket connection management
  useEffect(() => {
    const ws = new WebSocket(`${WS_URL}/osce/${sessionId}`);

    ws.onopen = () => {
      setIsConnected(true);
      console.log('WebSocket connected');
    };

    ws.onmessage = (event) => {
      const data = JSON.parse(event.data);

      if (data.type === 'message') {
        setMessages(prev => [...prev, {
          id: data.id,
          sender: 'ai',
          content: data.content,
          timestamp: Date.now()
        }]);
        setIsTyping(false);
      } else if (data.type === 'typing') {
        setIsTyping(true);
      }
    };

    ws.onerror = (error) => {
      console.error('WebSocket error:', error);
      setIsConnected(false);
    };

    ws.onclose = () => {
      setIsConnected(false);
      console.log('WebSocket disconnected');
      // TODO: Implement auto-reconnect with exponential backoff
    };

    wsRef.current = ws;

    return () => {
      ws.close();
    };
  }, [sessionId]);

  // Auto-scroll to latest message
  useEffect(() => {
    messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });
  }, [messages]);

  const handleSendMessage = useCallback(() => {
    if (!inputValue.trim() || !wsRef.current || !isConnected) return;

    const message: Message = {
      id: crypto.randomUUID(),
      sender: 'user',
      content: inputValue,
      timestamp: Date.now()
    };

    setMessages(prev => [...prev, message]);
    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({
      type: 'message',
      content: inputValue
    }));
    setInputValue('');
  }, [inputValue, isConnected]);

  return (
    <Box sx={{ height: '100vh', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
      {/* Connection status */}
      {!isConnected && (
        <Alert severity="warning">Disconnected. Attempting to reconnect...</Alert>
      )}

      {/* Message list */}
      <Paper sx={{ flex: 1, overflow: 'auto', p: 2 }}>
        {messages.map(msg => (
          <Box
            key={msg.id}
            sx={{
              mb: 2,
              textAlign: msg.sender === 'user' ? 'right' : 'left'
            }}
          >
            <Typography
              sx={{
                display: 'inline-block',
                p: 1.5,
                borderRadius: 2,
                bgcolor: msg.sender === 'user' ? 'primary.main' : 'grey.200',
                color: msg.sender === 'user' ? 'white' : 'text.primary'
              }}
            >
              {msg.content}
            </Typography>
          </Box>
        ))}

        {isTyping && (
          <Box sx={{ textAlign: 'left' }}>
            <CircularProgress size={20} />
            <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ ml: 1 }}>AI is typing...</Typography>
          </Box>
        )}

        <div ref={messagesEndRef} />
      </Paper>

      {/* Message input */}
      <Box sx={{ p: 2, display: 'flex', gap: 1 }}>
        <TextField
          fullWidth
          value={inputValue}
          onChange={(e) => setInputValue(e.target.value)}
          onKeyPress={(e) => e.key === 'Enter' && handleSendMessage()}
          placeholder="Type your message..."
          disabled={!isConnected}
          aria-label="Message input"
        />
        <Button
          variant="contained"
          onClick={handleSendMessage}
          disabled={!isConnected || !inputValue.trim()}
        >
          Send
        </Button>
      </Box>
    </Box>
  );
};
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ **DON'T**: Hardcode WebSocket URLs
```typescript
const ws = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:8001/ws');
```

✅ **DO**: Use environment variables
```typescript
const WS_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_WEBSOCKET_URL;
const ws = new WebSocket(`${WS_URL}/osce/${sessionId}`);
```

❌ **DON'T**: Use `any` types
```typescript
const [messages, setMessages] = useState<any[]>([]);
```

✅ **DO**: Define proper interfaces
```typescript
interface Message {
  id: string;
  sender: 'user' | 'ai';
  content: string;
  timestamp: number;
}
const [messages, setMessages] = useState<Message[]>([]);
```

❌ **DON'T**: Render unsanitized user input
```typescript
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: msg.content }} />
```

✅ **DO**: Use Material-UI components (auto-escapes)
```typescript
<Typography>{msg.content}</Typography>
```
